==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|hursan|horse|lang=ang}} (perhaps from a form ''*hrussa-'' ‘runner, racer’), from {{proto|Indo-European|kers-|run|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|hors|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|hros|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|ros|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|hros|lang=goh}}, {{term|ros|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Ross|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hross|lang=non}} (whence the Old Swedish ''hors'' and Icelandic {{term|hross|lang=is}}); and, outside the Germanic languages, with Latin {{term|curro|currō|run, race|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hors/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=n}}

# [[horse]]

